A test files for Qore::Process module.

Always run process.qtest file. That's the main one.

On Linux, run the deterministic process-state regression against the local module:

    python3 -B -W error test/run-process-state.py --module build/process-api-2.0.qmod
    python3 -B -W error test/run-process-state.py --module build-debug/process-api-2.0.qmod --valgrind

The test interposer models disappearance between kill(pid, 0) and /proc inspection,
including removal after opening the stat file. It also checks zombie/dead states,
permission errors, an unavailable proc filesystem, malformed data and live states.
It affects only the test process's own stat lookup and is never installed.

The other *.q files are supporting helpers for I/O and environment handling.
